They corner Nebula near the far side.

But then Nebula opens a containment device.

Inside is the stolen shadow.

It pours out like black smoke.

For one glorious moment, Cage becomes silhouetted against Earth.

He loves it.

Jessica:

“Do not fucking pose right now.”

Cage:

“I wasn’t.”

Little Nick:

“You absolutely were.”

Nebula activates the machine.

The entire moon starts going dark.

Cage realizes the truth.

Nebula isn’t stealing shadows.

He’s manufacturing them.

Jessica:

“Why?”

Nebula spreads his arms.

“Because Earth has too much light.”

Cage:

“That’s stupid.”

Nebula:

“Privacy is the new oil.”

Little Nick:

“…That’s actually kind of hard.”

Jessica:

“Don’t encourage the villain.”

Nebula launches a shadow beam toward Earth.

Cage looks at Little Nick.

Little Nick looks at Cage.

Both:

“The Quarter.”

Jessica:

“NO.”

Cage flips the Quarter.

It floats.

Because moon gravity.

It keeps spinning.

For thirty seconds.

Everyone just watches.

Nebula:

“Is this part of your plan?”

Cage:

“Potentially.”

The Quarter lands on its edge.

Little Nick screams:

“THIRD OPTION.”

Cage immediately shoots the moon.

Jessica:

“WHAT THE FUCK WAS THAT SUPPOSED TO DO?”

One bullet travels slowly across the lunar surface.

Hits an old golf ball.

Golf ball ricochets into a discarded wrench.

Wrench hits Nebula’s control panel.

Shadow machine shuts off.

Everyone is silent.

Cage lowers pistol.

“Police work.”

Jessica:

“No. No, we are not calling that police work.”

Micro Nick emerges from Cage’s breast pocket.

“Admissible.”

Jessica:

“YOU SHUT THE FUCK UP TOO.”

